st 21 percent had a positive view of  polyeth the key takeaway for us here is  that uh conservative party members have  a clear choice between two different  strategies go with the populist favorite  of the party's base like pauliev or pick  a leader like cheray who may have more  potential to appeal to voters outside  the party  one thing for conservatives to consider  that moderate image that aaron o'toole  presented in last summer's election was  in fact a big problem at one point for  the trudeau liberals at the start of the  campaign there was a lot of potential  that came from that that moderate appeal  dan arnold was the pollster inside the  liberal election war room in 2021 and he  says there was a point in the last  campaign when he was telling the trudeau  team they were on the path to lose to a  moderate conservative certainly the  trajectory the way things were going was  uh was headed to a very unpleasant place  from uh from our perspective there and  that is the campaign's divide right now  capture the base or broaden the base now  as for leslie lewis patrick brown and  the others in the race the ipsos poll  says the vast majority of canadians  simply do not know enough about them yet  to have an opinion donna  all right david in ottawa thanks  priceless advice ahead some tips on  navigating the soaring cost of living  [Music]  hearing that canada's inflation rate in  march was 6.7 percent is probably not a  huge shock for a lot of people because  of course people are living it the price  of almost everything is up and interest  rates are rising too managing your money  is getting trickier with me is pamela  george she's a personal finance  counselor pamela thanks for for speaking  with us you know everyone's personal  circumstances are different of course  but let's start with the broad strokes  for people carrying lots of credit and  mortgage debt who got used to low  interest rates and now see that is  rising plus inflation what is the first  thing 